s it), stage 3 open league with rl-v2 too. rl-v1 learned to beat az-v1 only once az-v1 was in its league.","rejected":"Self-play only; one flat league."},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:40:00","kind":"decision","title":"Start from rl-v1's checkpoint, widened with the helper inputs","text":"rl-v1 r2 was still improving when it stopped (67% to 81% vs GA over 2,200 iterations), and the helper inputs lifted rl-v2 by 3 points. Weights and Adam state loaded; new inputs at zero weight.","rejected":"From zero (rl-v2 plateaued at ~74%); imitation of the GA (rl-v1 already did that)."},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:34:49","kind":"stage_pass","stage":"champion","index":1,"iter":78,"why":"eval champion 0.583 >= 0.56","champion":"runs/c1/net_78.npy","eval":"GA 0.815 champ 0.583 BM 0.905 Smithy 0.875 Witch 0.750 bots 0.843","run":"c1"},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:34:49","kind":"stage_start","stage":"open league","index":2,"iter":79,"expect":"Every earlier model, so beating the champion does not cost strength elsewhere.","run":"c1"},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:30:00","kind":"decision","title":"No chain module in the player","text":"The released player is the network alone. On the chain exam rl-v1's champion picks the coin-best action 91.6% of the time, but with a turn planner (value judge or coins judge, K=32) or a chain rule choosing its actions it scored 48.8%, 48.5%, 48.2% (engine kingdoms) and 49.9% head to head against itself without it.","rejected":"A statistical turn planner at play time (no gain, 20x slower); a hand-written chain rule (changed 15 of 6,335 decisions)."},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:16:53","kind":"goal_best","iter":46,"check":{"score":0.8575,"n":400},"champion":"runs/c1/net_46.npy","eval":"GA 0.858 champ 0.465 BM 0.950 Smithy 0.870 Witch 0.775 bots 0.865","run":"c1"},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:02:40","kind":"run_resume","iter":25,"stage":"champion","run":"c1"},{"t":"2026-11-19T09:02:36","kind":"note","text":"Card school added to stages 2 and 3 (15% of games: first buys forced to an under-used card, not recorded)